WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.861 --> 00:00:05.029
Line 3 has to stand in hall B before the summer shutdown ends.

2
00:00:05.745 --> 00:00:09.333
Plan and materials are right, but the line stands still.

3
00:00:10.354 --> 00:00:11.619
Nobody knows why.

4
00:00:12.307 --> 00:00:15.964
You lead the project, and the sponsor wants to know what is going on.

5
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.173
We follow this project through the four topics of the module.

6
00:00:20.874 --> 00:00:23.394
The details come later, in the lessons.

7
00:00:24.735 --> 00:00:27.638
The first topic is Diagnosing why it is stuck.

8
00:00:28.389 --> 00:00:29.805
Which kind of stuck is it?

9
00:00:30.894 --> 00:00:32.601
There are four kinds of stuck.

10
00:00:33.414 --> 00:00:37.860
An unclear goal, an unclear way, a people problem or a capacity problem.

11
00:00:38.881 --> 00:00:42.132
Ask four questions, and start at the first no.

12
00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.925
The goal and the way are clear, but the team lead does not give his support.

13
00:00:47.751 --> 00:00:49.063
That is a people problem.

14
00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:54.691
A diagnosis based on a feeling convinces nobody, so you look for the facts.

15
00:00:55.693 --> 00:00:59.164
For the facts we use triangulation and a decision log.

16
00:01:00.499 --> 00:01:02.763
The second topic is When you do not know.

17
00:01:03.473 --> 00:01:05.876
The sponsor asks something you do not know.

18
00:01:06.586 --> 00:01:07.561
What do you say then?

19
00:01:08.554 --> 00:01:11.445
The sponsor asks when line 3 runs again.

20
00:01:12.135 --> 00:01:13.029
You do not know.

21
00:01:13.725 --> 00:01:15.641
Say so, and say when you will.

22
00:01:16.374 --> 00:01:19.671
When the answer comes on that day, it builds trust.

23
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:24.140
Separate what you know, what you think and what you do not know yet.

24
00:01:24.948 --> 00:01:25.645
Never bluff.

25
00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:30.231
When you do not know we use a holding statement and a range.

26
00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:34.241
The third topic is Resistance and politics.

27
00:01:34.954 --> 00:01:38.286
The team lead says it is a good idea, but not right now.

28
00:01:38.987 --> 00:01:41.135
People rarely block with a hard no.

29
00:01:42.139 --> 00:01:45.413
Pushing or working around him usually makes it worse.

30
00:01:46.146 --> 00:01:47.992
Start by understanding why.

31
00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.891
Maybe he fears that line 4 will struggle if his crew goes away.

32
00:01:53.861 --> 00:01:56.566
Talk one to one and ask what makes it hard.

33
00:01:57.323 --> 00:02:00.829
If that fails, you escalate, and you tell him first.

34
00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.685
For this we use the three levels of resistance.

35
00:02:05.971 --> 00:02:08.641
The fourth topic is Restarting with the sponsor.

36
00:02:09.376 --> 00:02:10.932
What do you need from your sponsor?

37
00:02:12.011 --> 00:02:15.018
A sponsor can usually get a stuck project moving.

38
00:02:15.706 --> 00:02:19.839
He decides, makes room and gives air cover, but only if you ask.

39
00:02:20.857 --> 00:02:23.399
Ask concretely, with a name and a date.

40
00:02:24.159 --> 00:02:28.280
Will you tell the team lead on Monday that the crew is free one day a week?

41
00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.463
To restart we use a sponsor check-in.

42
00:02:32.784 --> 00:02:33.632
It connects.

43
00:02:34.343 --> 00:02:37.815
You look for the facts, you stay honest about what you do not know,

44
00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.708
and you talk to the team lead.

45
00:02:40.456 --> 00:02:42.070
Then the sponsor decides.

46
00:02:43.081 --> 00:02:45.856
The sponsor says it to the team lead on Monday.

47
00:02:46.578 --> 00:02:49.724
The crew is free again, and line 3 gets moving.

48
00:02:50.451 --> 00:02:52.506
The decision is on the decision log.

49
00:02:53.867 --> 00:02:55.516
This is the map of Projects.

50
00:02:56.236 --> 00:02:59.940
When you are stuck is the first station of People and influence.

51
00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:04.306
This module has four topics, each with four levels.

52
00:03:05.293 --> 00:03:08.683
Start with Diagnosing why it is stuck, at Basics level.

53
00:03:09.692 --> 00:03:13.117
At Working knowledge you add getting facts, asking for help,

54
00:03:13.338 --> 00:03:15.172
client pressure and small wins.

55
00:03:16.181 --> 00:03:21.139
At Advanced you add deeper causes, uncertainty, the pocket veto and the reset.

56
00:03:22.207 --> 00:03:25.469
At Expert you add the project review, the kind of problem,

57
00:03:25.585 --> 00:03:27.837
stuck departments and a red project.

58
00:03:28.878 --> 00:03:33.069
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
